# PR-Agent workflow (mdeapp)

Shipped in PR #236 (merged). Upstream: [The-PR-Agent/pr-agent](https://github.com/The-PR-Agent/pr-agent) · docs: [docs.pr-agent.ai](https://docs.pr-agent.ai/).

**Role:** Third automated review lane for Sofía — alongside Cursor Bugbot and CodeRabbit. Helpful for `/describe`, `/review`, and `/improve` on PRs to `main`. **Not** a merge blocker unless you wire it into branch protection (today: informational + Actions check only).

## What runs automatically

Workflow: `.github/workflows/pr-agent.yml`

| Trigger | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| PR **opened**, **synchronize**, or **reopened** targeting `main` | GitHub Actions job **PR Agent** (`pr_agent_job`) |
| Sender is a **bot** | Skipped (`github.event.sender.type != 'Bot'`) — avoids loops with Bugbot / CodeRabbit |

| Setting | Value |
|---------|--------|
| Action pin | `the-pr-agent/pr-agent@v0.36.0` |
| Secret | `OPENAI_KEY` (repo Actions secret) |
| Token | Default `GITHUB_TOKEN` (no manual secret) |
| Permissions | `pull-requests: write`, `issues: write`, `contents: read` |

Verify: `gh pr checks <PR#> | rg -i 'pr.agent|pr_agent'`

## Manual tools (PR comments)

Comment on the **PR** (not issue) to re-run or invoke a specific tool:

| Command | Use when |
|---------|----------|
| `/review` | Full PR review — bugs, risks, suggestions |
| `/describe` | Auto-generate or refresh PR title + description |
| `/improve` | Actionable code-improvement suggestions |
| `/ask <question>` | Q&A about the PR diff |
| `/help` | List available tools |

Docs: [Review](https://docs.pr-agent.ai/tools/review/) · [Describe](https://docs.pr-agent.ai/tools/describe/) · [Improve](https://docs.pr-agent.ai/tools/improve/) · [Ask](https://docs.pr-agent.ai/tools/ask/)

**Agent habit:** After opening a PR, scan PR-Agent comments the same way as CodeRabbit/cubic — fix P0/P1 or document wont-fix in evidence.

## Local CLI (optional)

For pre-PR review without waiting on Actions:

```bash
pip install pr-agent
export OPENAI_KEY=...   # never commit; use your own key locally
pr-agent --pr_url https://github.com/amo-tech-ai/mdeapp/pull/<N> review
```

Other tools: append `describe`, `improve`, or `ask` instead of `review`. See [CLI usage](https://docs.pr-agent.ai/usage-guide/automations_and_usage/#local-repo-cli).

## How PR-Agent fits with other reviewers

| Tool | When | Agent action |
|------|------|----------------|
| **Bugbot** | Before push; `cursor review` on PR | Subagent `/review-bugbot` — see `bugbot.mdc` |
| **CodeRabbit** | Pre-PR CLI + post-open threads | Skill `coderabbit` |
| **cubic** | Pre-PR CLI + CI | Skill `run-review` |
| **PR-Agent** | Auto on PR + `/review` etc. on demand | Read PR comments; fix or wont-fix |

**Do not** treat three bots as one — triage separately. Floor + Vercel remain the **required** merge gates.

## Optional repo config

Add `.pr_agent.toml` at repo root only when you need model or tool tuning — see [configuration](https://docs.pr-agent.ai/usage-guide/configuration/). Default OpenAI model comes from PR-Agent + `OPENAI_KEY`. Production app AI stays **Gemini-only** (`src/**`); PR-Agent OpenAI usage is **CI-only**.

## mdeapp habits

- One PR closes one `SAN-NNN` only — pair full Linear title in PR body.
- Small focused PRs (≤15 files) get better `/review` signal — see `mde-worktree-pr-flow`.
- Do not paste secrets into PR comments or `.pr_agent.toml` commits.
- After applying PR-Agent `/improve` suggestions, re-run targeted `npm test` and browser proof if UI changed (`mdeai-real-world-proof-pr-review.mdc`).

## When agents should load this rule

- User mentions PR-Agent, `/review`, `/describe`, `/improve` on a PR
- Debugging why **PR Agent** Actions job failed (missing `OPENAI_KEY`, permissions, bot skip)
- Adding or changing `.github/workflows/pr-agent.yml` or `.pr_agent.toml`
